{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>If he rises and walks about.</b> But if he does not rise and remains bedridden with illness a long time and dies of that illness — the striker is put to death." "<b>Upon his staff.</b> His cane, as in 'and take my staff in your hand' regarding Elisha, in the manner of those who recover from illness." "<b>His rest he shall give.</b> The time of his sitting idle from work, as in 'this house rested a little.' And a proof for the matter: 'if he rises and walks about outside.'" "<b>He shall give.</b> Even if he healed without blemish."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:26.414679440Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}